WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.797
Once the patient-admission interface exists, later reports can start from it.

00:00:05.797 --> 00:00:09.852
This query groups the reusable admission rows by department.

00:00:09.852 --> 00:00:15.457
The report author does not need to repeat patient joins or stay-duration calculations.

00:00:15.457 --> 00:00:23.322
That is the value of modular SQL: stable logic is centralized, and consumer queries become smaller.

00:00:23.322 --> 00:00:28.717
A standard view stores a query definition, not a separate copy of the rows.

00:00:28.717 --> 00:00:34.922
Treat the selected columns, names, types, and grain as a contract with downstream users.

00:00:34.922 --> 00:00:41.443
Changing that contract can break dashboards or applications even if the underlying query still runs.
